<title>USA: Eastern Utilities Associates Q4 net slips.</title>
<headline>Eastern Utilities Associates Q4 net slips.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>				     Dec 31	 Dec 31     Increase</p>
<p>					 1996	  1995    (Decrease)</p>
<p> Operating Revenues    $138,406,625 $135,327,005   $3,079,620</p>
<p>Consolidated Earnings</p>
<p>Applicable to EUA</p>
<p>  Common Shares	     7,735,009   10,411,378  (2,676,369)</p>
<p> Average shares	    20,435,997   20,404,415	 31,582</p>
<p>Consolidated Earnings</p>
<p>   Per Share			 0.38	   0.51	 (0.13)</p>
<p>				     12 Months Ended</p>
<p>				  Dec 31	   Dec 31     Increase</p>
<p>				   1996	     1995     (Decrease)</p>
<p> Operating Revenues $527,067,784   $563,362,820 $(36,295,036)</p>
<p>Consolidated Earnings</p>
<p>Applicable to EUA</p>
<p>  Common Shares	 30,613,872     32,626,052   (2,012,180)</p>
<p> Average Shares	 20,436,217     20,238,961	 197,256</p>
<p>Consolidated Earnings</p>
<p>   Per Share		 1.50	   1.61		 (0.11)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 year includes after-tax charge of $3.7 million (18 cents per share) related to Cogenex write-offs.</p>
<p>1995  year includes one-time, after-tax, charge of $10.5 million (52 cents per share) related to discontinuance of cogeneration operations by EUA Cogenex Corp and after-tax charge of $2.7 million (14 cents per share) related to a voluntary retirement incentive offer.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
